# Tinga Bowl

Based on [https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/chicken-tinga-bowls/](https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/chicken-tinga-bowls) ([wayback](http://web.archive.org/web/20260129194822/https://www.halfbakedharvest.com/chicken-tinga-bowls/)) and [https://www.chilipeppermadness.com/recipes/chicken-tinga/](https://www.chilipeppermadness.com/recipes/chicken-tinga/)

{ rating="0" image="None" }
:::
:::

## Ingredients

### Tinga Sauce

- [ ] 1 (14.5 oz) can [fire-roasted diced tomatoes]{ ing="fire-roasted-diced-tomatoes" }
- [ ] 2-3 [chipotle peppers]{ ing="chipotle-peppers" } in adobo sauce, plus 2 Tbsp adobo sauce
- [ ] 3 cloves [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [dried oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }
- [ ] 1 tsp [ground cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }
- [ ] 1/2 tsp [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }
- [ ] [Salt and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } to taste

### Protein (choose one)

- [ ] 1.5 lbs [boneless chicken thighs]{ ing="boneless-chicken-thighs" }, cut into strips or shredded after cooking
- [ ] 1.5 lbs [ground turkey]{ ing="ground-turkey" }
- [ ] 1.5 lbs [extra-firm tofu]{ ing="extra-firm-tofu" }, pressed and cubed

### Aromatics and Vegetables

- [ ] 1 large [yellow onion]{ ing="yellow-onion" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 [red bell pepper]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 1 [green bell pepper]{ ing="green-bell-pepper" }, thinly sliced
- [ ] 2 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="olive-oil" }

### Cilantro-Lime Brown Rice

- [ ] 1.5 cups [long-grain brown rice]{ ing="long-grain-brown-rice" }
- [ ] 2.5 cups [water or chicken broth]{ ing="water-or-chicken-broth" }
- [ ] [Juice of 2 limes]{ ing="juice-of-2-limes" }
- [ ] 1/4 cup fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] 1 Tbsp [butter or olive oil]{ ing="butter-or-olive-oil" }
- [ ] [Salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

### Bowl Toppings

- [ ] 1 (15 oz) can [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, drained and rinsed
- [ ] 1 cup [corn]{ ing="corn" } (fresh, frozen, or canned)
- [ ] 1-2 [avocados]{ ing="avocados" }, sliced
- [ ] 1/2 cup [queso fresco]{ ing="queso-fresco" } or cotija cheese, crumbled
- [ ] 1/4 cup [pickled jalapeños]{ ing="pickled-jalape-os" }
- [ ] Fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, chopped
- [ ] [Lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }
- [ ] Chipotle crema: 1/4 cup [sour cream]{ ing="sour-cream" } or Greek yogurt mixed with 1 tsp adobo sauce

## Recipe

### Make the Tinga Sauce

1. In a blender, combine fire-roasted [tomatoes]{ ing="fire-roasted-diced-tomatoes" }, [chipotle peppers]{ ing="chipotle-peppers" }, adobo sauce, [garlic]{ ing="garlic" }, [oregano]{ ing="dried-oregano" }, [cumin]{ ing="ground-cumin" }, [smoked paprika]{ ing="smoked-paprika" }, [salt]{ ing="salt" }, [and pepper]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" }
1. Blend until smooth. Set aside

### Cook the Rice

1. Rinse [brown rice]{ ing="long-grain-brown-rice" } until water runs clear
1. In a pot or [rice]{ ing="long-grain-brown-rice" } cooker, combine rice and water/[broth]{ ing="water-or-chicken-broth" }. Bring to a boil, reduce heat to low, cover, and simmer for 40-45 minutes
1. Remove from heat, let sit covered for 10 minutes, then fluff with a fork
1. Stir in [lime]{ ing="juice-of-2-limes" } juice, [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }, butter/[oil]{ ing="butter-or-olive-oil" }, and [salt]{ ing="salt" } to taste

### Cook the Protein and Vegetables

1. Heat 2 Tbsp [olive oil]{ ing="butter-or-olive-oil" } in a large skillet or Dutch oven over medium-high heat
1. Add sliced [onions]{ ing="yellow-onion" } and [bell peppers]{ ing="red-bell-pepper" }. Cook until softened, 5-6 minutes. Remove and set aside
1. In the same pan, add protein:

   - For chicken: Cook chicken strips 5-6 minutes until cooked through (or shred pre-cooked chicken and add)
   - For ground turkey: Cook, breaking up with a spoon, until browned, 6-8 minutes
   - For tofu: Cook cubes 4-5 minutes, stirring occasionally, until golden
1. Pour tinga sauce over the protein. Add [onions]{ ing="yellow-onion" } [and peppers]{ ing="salt-and-pepper" } back to the pan
1. Reduce heat to medium-low and simmer for 10-15 minutes, allowing flavors to meld and sauce to thicken slightly
1. If using [chicken thighs]{ ing="boneless-chicken-thighs" } whole, shred with two forks after simmering

### Warm the Black Beans and Corn

1. In a small pot, warm [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" } and [corn]{ ing="corn" } together over medium heat, 3-4 minutes. Season with [salt]{ ing="salt" }

### Assemble Bowls

1. Divide [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }-[lime]{ ing="juice-of-2-limes" } [rice]{ ing="long-grain-brown-rice" } among serving bowls
1. Top with tinga (protein with sauce), [black beans]{ ing="black-beans" }, and [corn]{ ing="corn" }
1. Add sliced [avocado]{ ing="avocados" }, crumbled [queso fresco]{ ing="queso-fresco" }, [pickled jalapeños]{ ing="pickled-jalape-os" }, and fresh [cilantro]{ ing="cilantro" }
1. Drizzle with chipotle crema and serve with [lime wedges]{ ing="lime-wedges" }

## Notes

- **Traditional preparation:** Often uses white rice, which cooks in 15-20 minutes and has a lighter, fluffier texture
- **Flavor/texture tradeoff with brown rice:** Brown rice is chewier and nuttier. The lime juice and cilantro help keep it fresh and bright. For a lighter texture, use white rice or a 50/50 blend
- **Spice level:** Start with 2 chipotle peppers and add more to taste. The adobo sauce adds flavor without too much heat
- **Sheet pan method:** For easier cleanup, toss chicken/tofu, onions, and peppers with tinga sauce and roast at 425F for 20-25 minutes
- **Make ahead:** Tinga sauce can be made 3-5 days ahead. Cooked tinga lasts 3-4 days refrigerated or 3 months frozen
- **Meal prep:** Store components separately. Tinga and rice reheat well. Add fresh toppings when serving
- **Protein variations:** Shredded rotisserie chicken works great for a quick version. Ground beef or pork also work well
- Related to [Burrito](./burrito.html) and [Cauliflower Lime Burrito Bowl](./cauliflower_lime_burrito_bowl.html)
